PART 5: RESUME SCANNABILITY MATRIX (THE 7.4-SECOND SCALPEL)
Hiring managers scan resumes for an average of 7.4 seconds before rendering an initial triage decision. Erase prose-heavy paragraphs within past roles; optimize layouts purely for rapid vertical scannability.
- The First-Person Summary Pivot: Erase dry, machine-generated lists of bulleted tools at the header. Replace them with a punchy, highly concise first-person statement showcasing clear business metrics, system scaling values, and operational outcomes up front.
- Company Name Dominance: Human screeners look for institutional authority. Lead all line entries loudly with the Company Name on official system record.
- Ruthless Chronological Trimming: Allocate 90% of the visual layout space to achievements within the last 5 years. Condense legacy history down to highly brief, high-impact lines highlighting major structural milestones.
- Age-Profiling De-biasing Shield: Strip chronological dating tags, graduation years, and foundational timelines from all education and certification blocks, defining professional identity entirely by active capability footprints.

